            <ArticleTitle>Transradial coronary angiography with virtual 1 French, sheathless 3 French catheter.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>E676-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/ccd.24885</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Minimizing catheter size can reduce bleeding complications in coronary angiography. We herein report extreme slender &quot;needle size&quot; (19-G) coronary diagnostic catheterization using a new 3-Fr diagnostic catheter by sheathless method. A 58-year-old man having effort angina underwent coronary angiography. The 3-Fr Ikari Left diagnostic catheter, which is equal to 19-G, was inserted smoothly both for left and right coronary arteries by sheathless method. We only needed 4 min to achieve hemostasis with manual compression after catheter withdrawal in this case.</AbstractText>
